  "result": "Fixed! The issue was that users were receiving notifications about their own comments. The problem was in the `comment.created` subscription handler in the notification service, which was sending notifications to all watchers (issue author and assignee) without filtering out the person who created the comment.\n\nI've updated the code to:\n1. Filter out the comment author (`payload.actorId`) from the watchers list before sending notifications\n2. Also filter out the actor from the mention notifications, so they don't get notified if they mention themselves\n\nNow notifications will only go to other watchers and mentioned users, not to the person who created the comment.",
